* LM358B Dual Operational Amplifier SPICE Macromodel
* High-Fidelity Behavioral & Equivalent Circuit Representation

* Single Amplifier Subcircuit Definition

* Top-Level LM358B Macromodel Subcircuit

* --- Globally Hoisted Models for Multi-Subcircuit Visibility ---
.model S_MODEL VSWITCH (RON=10 ROFF=1G VTH=0.5 VH=0.1)
.model D_PROT D (IS=1e-15 N=1 RS=10)
.model PMOS PMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.7 KP=40u GAMMA=0.5 PHI=0.8 LAMBDA=0.01)
.model NMOS NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=0.7 KP=100u GAMMA=0.4 PHI=0.7 LAMBDA=0.01)

.subckt LM358B_AMP OUT IN_N IN_P VEE VCC
* Input bias currents (PNP inputs sink current out of pins, ~10 nA typical)
I_IBP IN_P VEE 10n
I_IBN IN_N VEE 10n

* Input Differential and Common-Mode Impedance
R_DIFF IN_P IN_N 10MEG
C_DIFF IN_P IN_N 1.5p
R_CM1  IN_P VEE 4G
R_CM2  IN_N VEE 4G
C_CM1  IN_P VEE 2p
C_CM2  IN_N VEE 2p

* Common-Mode and Power-Supply Rejection Modeling
* Internal reference mid-rail node
R_REF1 VCC MID 100k
R_REF2 MID VEE 100k
C_REF  MID VEE 10p

* Input Common-Mode Voltage Detection
E_VCM VCM_NODE 0 VALUE = { 0.5*(V(IN_P) + V(IN_N)) }
* Supply variation detection (PSRR: 100 dB -> 10uV/V)
E_VPS VPS_NODE 0 VALUE = { (V(VCC) - V(VEE) - 5.0) * 3.16e-6 }
* Common-mode variation detection (CMRR: 90 dB -> 3.16e-5 V/V)
E_VCMR VCMR_NODE 0 VALUE = { (V(VCM_NODE) - V(MID)) * 1.0e-5 }

* Input Offset and Error Summing
E_DIFF IN_INT 0 VALUE = { V(IN_P) - V(IN_N) + 0.0003 + V(VPS_NODE) + V(VCMR_NODE) }

* Slew-Rate Limited Transconductance Stage
* Slew Rate = 0.5 V/us = 5e5 V/s. With C_comp = 20 pF, I_max = 10 uA.
* gm = 2*pi * GBW * C_comp = 2*pi * 1.2MHz * 20pF = 1.508e-4 S.
* Linear range of diff input = 10uA / 1.508e-4 = 66.3 mV.
G_GM1 VEE N_GM VALUE = { 10u * tanh(V(IN_INT) / 0.0663) }
R_GM1 N_GM VEE 10MEG
C_GM1 N_GM VEE 20p

* High Gain Stage
* DC gain = AOL >= 140,000 (103 dB).
* First stage gain: gm * R_GM1 = 1.508e-4 * 10MEG = 1508.
* Second stage gain needed = 140000 / 1508 = 92.84.
E_GAIN N_A2 VEE VALUE = { V(N_GM, VEE) * 9.284 }
R_A2 N_A2 N_INT 1k
C_A2 N_INT VEE 10p

* LM358 Output Rail Saturation & Sinking Behavior
* Positive limit: VCC - 1.35V
* Negative limit: VEE + 5mV (down to low mV range when sourcing no current)
E_OUT_IDEAL N_LIM VEE VALUE = { min(V(VCC) - V(VEE) - 1.35, +     max(0.005, V(N_INT, VEE))) }

* Output Driver with Current Limiting and Output Resistance
* Open-loop output resistance: 300 ohms. Short circuit limit ~ 40mA.
* Source limit: 40 mA, Sink limit: 30 mA.
B_OUT N_DRV VEE V = { V(N_LIM) }
R_OUT_INT N_DRV N_SENSE 150
R_OUT_EXT N_SENSE OUT 150

* Output Current Clamping
* When sourcing > 40mA or sinking > 30mA, clamp via feedback current
B_CLAMP OUT VEE I = { (V(N_SENSE, OUT) > 6.0) ? (V(N_SENSE, OUT) - 6.0)*0.5 : + (V(N_SENSE, OUT) < -4.5) ? (V(N_SENSE, OUT) + 4.5)*0.5 : 0 }

* Quiescent Supply Current per Channel (~300 uA)
G_IQ VCC VEE VALUE = { 300u + 2.5u * (V(VCC) - V(VEE) - 5.0) }

.ends LM358B_AMP

.subckt LM358B OUT1 IN1 IN1_P V IN2_P IN2 OUT2 V_P
* Pin 1: OUT1
* Pin 2: IN1   (Negative input of amplifier 1)
* Pin 3: IN1_P (Positive input of amplifier 1)
* Pin 4: V     (Negative supply)
* Pin 5: IN2_P (Positive input of amplifier 2)
* Pin 6: IN2   (Negative input of amplifier 2)
* Pin 7: OUT2
* Pin 8: V_P   (Positive supply)

* Channel 1 Instance
X_AMP1 OUT1 IN1 IN1_P V V_P LM358B_AMP

* Channel 2 Instance
X_AMP2 OUT2 IN2 IN2_P V V_P LM358B_AMP

* Cross-channel decoupling and isolation
C_CROSS OUT1 OUT2 0.05p
R_CROSS OUT1 OUT2 100G

.ends LM358B